an></span></lightning-icon><!--render facet: 478:0--><span class="headlineTitleText" data-aura-rendered-by="479:0"><span data-aura-rendered-by="482:0" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText">What are Duo's IP ranges, hostnames, and data residency areas by deployment?</span></span></h1><!--render facet: 483:0--><p class="headlineInfo" data-aura-rendered-by="484:0"><div dir="ltr" data-aura-rendered-by="4:140;a" class="uiOutputRichText" data-aura-class="uiOutputRichText">Explore other <a class="headlineArticles" data-aura-rendered-by="5:140;a" rel="noopener">articles</a> on this topic.</div></p></section></div></div></div><div class="slds-grid slds-wrap slds-medium-nowrap slds-large-nowrap" data-aura-rendered-by="546:0"><div class="slds-col--padded slds-size--12-of-12 slds-medium-size--8-of-12 slds-large-size--8-of-12 comm-layout-column" data-aura-rendered-by="547:0"><div data-region-name="content" data-item-id="f4aebe7d-24f9-44d3-995a-6ba9479a491c" data-aura-rendered-by="540:0"><div data-priority="" data-item-id="6940dd00-f3eb-4d20-807d-f791cbe02e8a" class="ui-widget" data-aura-rendered-by="537:0"><div data-aura-rendered-by="503:0"><!--render facet: 508:0--><div class="article-column zoom slds-text-longform selfServiceArticleLayout" data-aura-rendered-by="509:0" data-aura-class="selfServiceArticleLayout"><article class="summary" data-aura-rendered-by="510:0"><!--render facet: 3:156;a--><h2 class="article-head selfServiceArticleHeaderDetail" data-aura-rendered-by="6:156;a" data-aura-class="selfServiceArticleHeaderDetail">What are Duo's IP ranges, hostnames, and data residency areas by deployment?</h2><div data-aura-rendered-by="10:156;a" class="selfServiceArticleHeaderDetail" data-aura-class="selfServiceArticleHeaderDetail"><p class="article-summary" data-aura-rendered-by="11:156;a">KB FAQ: A Duo Security Knowledge Base Article</p><div class="meta" data-aura-rendered-by="14:156;a"><ul class="metadata-list" data-aura-rendered-by="15:156;a"><li class="metadata-list-item date" data-aura-rendered-by="16:156;a"><lightning-icon icon-name="utility:clock" class="slds-icon-utility-clock timestamp-icon slds-button__icon slds-icon_container forceIcon" data-data-rendering-service-uid="91" data-aura-rendered-by="20:156;a" lwc-4897l11qtae-host="" data-aura-class="forceIcon"><span lwc-4897l11qtae="" style="--sds-c-icon-color-background: var(--slds-c-icon-color-background, transparent)" part="boundary"><lightning-primitive-icon lwc-4897l11qtae="" exportparts="icon" size="xx-small" variant="inverse" lwc-3r73shvslrr-host=""><svg focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 520 520" part="icon" lwc-3r73shvslrr="" data-key="clock" class="slds-icon slds-icon_xx-small"><g lwc-3r73shvslrr=""><path d="M260 20C128 20 20 128 20 260s108 240 240 240 240-108 240-240S392 20 260 20m0 420c-99 0-180-81-180-180S161 80 260 80s180 81 180 180-81 180-180 180m34-178c-3-3-4-7-4-11v-96c0-8-7-15-15-15h-30c-8 0-15 7-15 15v121c0 4 2 8 4 11l74 74c6 6 15 6 21 0l21-21c6-6 6-15 0-21z" lwc-3r73shvslrr=""></path></g></svg></lightning-primitive-icon></span></lightning-icon><span data-aura-rendered-by="23:156;a" class="uiOutputDate" data-aura-class="uiOutputDate">Nov 25, 2025</span></li><li class="metadata-list-item article-type" data-aura-rendered-by="24:156;a">Knowledge</li></ul></div></div></article><article class="content" data-aura-rendered-by="511:0"><div class="full forcePageBlock forceRecordLayout" data-aura-rendered-by="94:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlock forceRecordLayout"><fieldset class="test-id__section slds-section  slds-is-open full min-width-0 forcePageBlockSection forcePageBlockSectionView" data-aura-rendered-by="73:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockSection forcePageBlockSectionView"><legend class="legend" data-aura-rendered-by="75:192;a"><h3 class="slds-section__title  test-id__section-header-container" data-aura-rendered-by="76:192;a" data-target-reveals="sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.Title,sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.UrlName,sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.Answer__c"><button type="button" class="slds-button test-id__section-header-button slds-section__title-action" data-aura-rendered-by="86:192;a" aria-controls="4:192;a" aria-expanded="true"><!--render facet: 87:192;a--><lightning-icon icon-name="utility:chevrondown" class="slds-icon-utility-chevrondown test-id__section-header-icon section-icon slds-m-right_x-small slds-button__icon slds-icon_container forceIcon" data-data-rendering-service-uid="104" data-aura-rendered-by="82:192;a" lwc-4897l11qtae-host="" data-aura-class="forceIcon"><span lwc-4897l11qtae="" style="--sds-c-icon-color-background: var(--slds-c-icon-color-background, transparent)" part="boundary"><lightning-primitive-icon lwc-4897l11qtae="" exportparts="icon" size="xx-small" variant="inverse" lwc-7nohpd9g9ec-host=""><svg focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 520 520" part="icon" lwc-7nohpd9g9ec="" data-key="chevrondown" class="slds-icon slds-icon_xx-small"><g lwc-7nohpd9g9ec=""><path d="M476 178L271 385c-6 6-16 6-22 0L44 178c-6-6-6-16 0-22l22-22c6-6 16-6 22 0l161 163c6 6 16 6 22 0l161-162c6-6 16-6 22 0l22 22c5 6 5 15 0 21" lwc-7nohpd9g9ec=""></path></g></svg></lightning-primitive-icon></span></lightning-icon><span class="test-id__section-header-title" data-aura-rendered-by="83:192;a">Information</span><!--render facet: 90:192;a--></button></h3></legend><div class="test-id__section-content slds-section__content section__content" data-aura-rendered-by="91:192;a" id="4:192;a" aria-hidden="false" style="transition: none;"><div role="list" class="slds-form slds-form_stacked " data-aura-rendered-by="92:192;a"><div class="slds-grid slds-gutters_small full cols-1 forcePageBlockSectionRow" data-aura-rendered-by="24:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockSectionRow"><div role="listitem" data-target-selection-name="sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.Title" class="slds-col slds-grid slds-has-flexi-truncate  full forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView" data-aura-rendered-by="11:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView"><div class="slds-form-element slds-form-element_readonly slds-grow slds-hint-parent override--slds-form-element" data-aura-rendered-by="12:192;a"><div class="test-id__field-label-container slds-form-element__label" data-aura-rendered-by="13:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-label" data-aura-rendered-by="14:192;a">Title</span></div><div class="slds-form-element__control slds-grid itemBody" data-aura-rendered-by="16:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-value slds-form-element__static slds-grow  is-read-only" data-aura-rendered-by="17:192;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="9:192;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText">What are Duo's IP ranges, hostnames, and data residency areas by deployment?</span></span><!--render facet: 19:192;a--><!--render facet: 20:192;a--></div></div></div></div><div class="slds-grid slds-gutters_small full cols-1 forcePageBlockSectionRow" data-aura-rendered-by="45:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockSectionRow"><div role="listitem" data-target-selection-name="sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.UrlName" class="slds-col slds-grid slds-has-flexi-truncate  full forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView" data-aura-rendered-by="32:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView"><div class="slds-form-element slds-form-element_readonly slds-grow slds-hint-parent override--slds-form-element" data-aura-rendered-by="33:192;a"><div class="test-id__field-label-container slds-form-element__label" data-aura-rendered-by="34:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-label" data-aura-rendered-by="35:192;a">URL Name</span></div><div class="slds-form-element__control slds-grid itemBody" data-aura-rendered-by="37:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-value slds-form-element__static slds-grow  is-read-only" data-aura-rendered-by="38:192;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="30:192;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText">1337</span></span><!--render facet: 40:192;a--><!--render facet: 41:192;a--></div></div></div></div><div class="slds-grid slds-gutters_small full cols-1 forcePageBlockSectionRow" data-aura-rendered-by="69:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockSectionRow"><div role="listitem" data-target-selection-name="sfdc:RecordField.Knowledge__kav.Answer__c" class="slds-col slds-grid slds-has-flexi-truncate  full long-text forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView" data-aura-rendered-by="56:192;a" data-aura-class="forcePageBlockItem forcePageBlockItemView"><div class="slds-form-element slds-form-element_readonly slds-grow slds-hint-parent override--slds-form-element" data-aura-rendered-by="57:192;a"><div class="test-id__field-label-container slds-form-element__label" data-aura-rendered-by="58:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-label" data-aura-rendered-by="59:192;a">Answer</span></div><div class="slds-form-element__control slds-grid itemBody" data-aura-rendered-by="61:192;a"><span class="test-id__field-value slds-form-element__static slds-grow  is-read-only" data-aura-rendered-by="62:192;a"><div dir="ltr" class="slds-rich-text-editor__output uiOutputRichText forceOutputRichText selfServiceOutputRichTextWithSmartLinks" data-aura-rendered-by="53:192;a" data-aura-class="uiOutputRichText forceOutputRichText selfServiceOutputRichTextWithSmartLinks"><div data-aura-rendered-by="54:192;a">Duo services are highly available and geographically distributed for resilience and performance across multiple IP addresses from known IP ranges based on data residency. We do not recommend locking down your firewall to individual IP addresses because these can and do change over time.<br><br>To ensure uninterrupted access to Duo's cloud authentication service, administrators need to ensure that communication is allowed to reach all of the following Duo MFA service IP blocks for the data residency area for your deployment. Please see&nbsp;<a target="_blank" href="https://help.duo.com/s/article/2060">this article for information on how to find your deployment ID</a>.<br>&nbsp;
<table style="width: 500px;" border="1"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Data Residency (Jurisdiction)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">IP Ranges</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Duo Deployments</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">U.S.</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.145.240.0/25<br>			52.32.63.128/26<br>			54.236.251.192/26<br>			54.241.191.128/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO1, DUO2, DUO4, DUO5, DUO6, DUO7, DUO9, DUO10, DUO13, DUO14, DUO15, DUO16, DUO17, DUO18, DUO19, DUO20, DUO21, DUO22, DUO23, DUO24, DUO28, DUO31, DUO32, DUO33, DUO35, DUO36, DUO37, DUO39, DUO40, DUO41, DUO42, DUO44, DUO45, DUO49, DUO50, DUO52, DUO55, DUO56, DUO58, DUO60, DUO62, DUO63, DUO64, DUO65, DUO71, DUO72, DUO73, DUO74, DUO75, DUO76, DUO77, DUO78, DUO79, DUO80</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">EU</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.39.113.0/26<br>			52.19.127.192/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO3,&nbsp;DUO47, DUO57</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Central Europe (Germany / Switzerland)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">16.62.194.128/26<br>			52.59.243.192/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO38, DUO48</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Canada</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">35.182.14.128/26<br>			40.176.213.192/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO53</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Australia</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.25.48.128/26<br>			16.51.103.128/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO66</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Japan</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">15.168.49.0/26<br>			35.74.77.64/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO67</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Southeast Asia (Singapore / Indonesia)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.213.75.128/26<br>			43.218.17.64/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO68</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">India</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.110.73.128/26<br>			18.60.199.0/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO69</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">UK</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.40.93.64/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO70</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">UAE</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">51.112.11.128/26<br>			16.24.91.0/26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">DUO81</td></tr></tbody></table>
</div>

<div data-aura-rendered-by="54:192;a">&nbsp;
<div>You can further restrict communication to the above IPs over specific ports required by your Duo application (example:&nbsp;HTTPS on TCP/443 or LDAPS on TCP/636). The IP ranges listed above are used by our core MFA and API services<br><br><strong>Other IPs (such as those contacted by mobile devices, used for the Duo Admin Panel, SSO, Passwordless, Duo Desktop, and for <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://www.duo.com">www.duo.com</a>) are dynamic and subject to change.&nbsp; If your org has strict IP filtering in place, which Duo does not recommended, make sure to add the following URLs to firewall allow lists:</strong></div>

<ul><li>We <u><strong>strongly recommend</strong> </u>adding&nbsp;<span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;">*.<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://duosecurity.com">duosecurity.com</a></span>&nbsp;wildcard domain, which should encompass all the various components and URLs that Duo's service uses</li></ul>
In cases where the org doesn't allow top-level wildcard domains, adding the following sub-domains to the allow list should account for most traffic, however, due to the redundant and dynamic nature of our service, disruptions could still occur:

<ul><li>Duo SSO (non-custom domain):&nbsp; <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://sso-xxxxxxx.sso.duosecurity.com">sso-xxxxxxx.sso.duosecurity.com</a></span> or preferably *<span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;">.<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://sso.duosecurity.com">sso.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>Duo SSO (custom domain): URL of your custom domain (e.g.. <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://xxxxxx.login.duosecurity.com">xxxxxx.login.duosecurity.com</a></span>)</li><li>Custom Enrollment, Self-Service Portal (SSP), and Passwordless:&nbsp;*<span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;">.<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://login.duosecurity.com">login.duosecurity.com</a> </span>and<span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"> *.<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://pwl.duosecurity.com">pwl.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>Device Management:<span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"> *.<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li></ul>

<div><br>Organizations using SSL filtering&nbsp;may also need to add their account's API hostname to their allow list. You can find this value on any application's settings page in the Duo Admin Panel:</div>

<div><img width="500" src="/servlet/rtaImage?eid=ka0Vs000000tFzJ&amp;feoid=00N700000039b6e&amp;refid=0EM700000015tAF" height="163" alt="See value in the API hostname field"><br><br><strong>User Enrollment and Self-Service Portal</strong><br>If your organization uses Duo's prompt-based enrollment and/or the Self-Service Portal, you may need to add the following hostnames to your allow list, depending on the location of your organization's Duo deployment:</div>

<ul><li>JP deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ane1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ane1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>IND deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://as1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">as1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>ASEAN deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ase1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ase1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>AUS deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ase2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ase2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>Canada deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://cc1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">cc1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>Central Europe (Germany / Switzerland) deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ec1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ec1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>EU deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ew1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ew1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>UK deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ew2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ew2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>UAE deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://mc1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">mc1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>US deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ue1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">ue1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a>, <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://uw1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">uw1.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a>, <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://uw2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com">uw2.devicemanagement.duosecurity.com</a></span></li></ul>

<div><br><strong>Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access (formerly Azure Conditional Access)</strong><br>If your organization uses Duo's <a target="_blank" href="https://duo.com/docs/azure-ca">Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access (formerly Azure Conditional Access)</a>&nbsp;application, you may need to add the following Duo hostnames to your allow list, depending on the location of your organization's Duo deployment:</div>

<div>
<ul><li>Canada deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://cc1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">cc1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>EU deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ec1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">ec1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a>,</span><span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;">&nbsp;<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://eu-west.azureauth.duosecurity.com">eu-west.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>US deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://us.azureauth.duosecurity.com">us.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>AU deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ase2.azureauth.duosecurity.com">ase2.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>ASEAN deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ase1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">ase1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>JP deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ane1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">ane1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>UK deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://ew2.azureauth.duosecurity.com">ew2.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>IND deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://as1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">as1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li><li>UAE deployments: <span style="font-family: Courier New,Courier,monospace;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://mc1.azureauth.duosecurity.com">mc1.azureauth.duosecurity.com</a></span></li></ul>

<div><br><strong>Trusted Endpoints</strong><br>If your organization is applying&nbsp;<a target="_blank" href="https://duo.com/docs/trusted-endpoints">Trusted Endpoints policies</a>&nbsp;to mobile devices, you should open firewalls to traffic from these IP ranges:<br>&nbsp;</div>

<table style="width: 500px;" border="1"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Data Residency (Jurisdiction)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">IP Range(s)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">U.S.</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.56.32.240/29<br>			52.32.63.176/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">EMEA</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">52.19.127.200/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Central Europe (Germany / Switzerland)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">52.59.243.200/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Canada</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">35.182.14.128/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Australia</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.25.48.188/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Japan</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">35.74.77.124/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Southeast Asia (Singapore / Indonesia)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.213.75.172/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">India</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.110.73.188/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">U.K.</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.40.93.124/30</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">UAE</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">51.112.11.135/30</td></tr></tbody></table>
<br><strong>Additional Information</strong><br>Please reference our <a target="_blank" href="https://help.duo.com/s/article/business-continuity-guide">Guide to Business Continuity Preparedness</a> for information on how to understand, plan for, and react to different Duo service outage scenarios.</div>
</div></div></span><!--render facet: 64:192;a--><!--render facet: 65:192;a--></div></div></div></div></div></div></fieldset></div></article></div><div class="slds-pill_container--bare selfServiceArticleTopicList selfServiceArticleLayout" data-aura-rendered-by="523:0" data-aura-class="selfServiceArticleTopicList selfServiceArticleLayout"><span class="slds-pill" data-aura-rendered-by="1:147;a"><a data-special-link="true" href="/s/topic/0TO4u000000f17NGAQ/authentication-methods-experience" class="slds-pill__label forceTopicTopicLink" data-aura-rendered-by="4:147;a" data-aura-class="forceTopicTopicLink"><span class="slds-grid slds-wrap" data-aura-rendered-by="5:147;a"><span class="slds-col slds-truncate" data-aura-rendered-by="6:147;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="9:147;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText">Authentication Methods &amp; Experience</span></span><span class="slds-hide" data-aura-rendered-by="10:147;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="13:147;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText"></span></span></span></a></span><span class="slds-pill" data-aura-rendered-by="14:147;a"><a data-special-link="true" href="/s/topic/0TO4u000000f17OGAQ/security-privacy-service-reliability" class="slds-pill__label forceTopicTopicLink" data-aura-rendered-by="17:147;a" data-aura-class="forceTopicTopicLink"><span class="slds-grid slds-wrap" data-aura-rendered-by="18:147;a"><span class="slds-col slds-truncate" data-aura-rendered-by="19:147;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="22:147;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText">Security, Privacy, &amp; Service Reliability</span></span><span class="slds-hide" data-aura-rendered-by="23:147;a"><span data-aura-rendered-by="26:147;a" class="uiOutputText" data-aura-class="uiOutputText"></span></span></span></a></span><span class="slds-pill" data-aura-rendered-by="27:147;a"><a data-special-link="true" href="/s/topic/0TO4u000000f17SGAQ/data-privacy" class="slds-pill__label forceTopicTopicLink" data-aura-rendered